course: dictionary
lesson: 14924
title: Words for kitchen machines
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A refrigerator is a big kitchen machine that keeps food and drinks cold, so they stay fresh for longer. Most people just call it the fridge. «We put the milk back in the refrigerator.» The word tells you where the milk goes: into a machine that keeps it cool.
explain: Can you guess the meaning from the words around it? «Keep the cream refrigerated after you open it.» Refrigerated comes from refrigerator, so it means kept cold in a refrigerator. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Keep the cream kept cold in a refrigerator after you open it.» It still makes sense, so you have worked it out.
explain: A refrigerator is also a safety word. «Raw meat goes on the bottom shelf of the refrigerator.» Raw meat can drip, so putting it at the bottom stops it dripping onto other food. «Never hide in an old refrigerator.» Old fridges with locks can trap a child, so this is a rule to remember.
fact: A refrigerator is a kitchen machine that keeps food and drinks cool.
fact: In everyday talk, a refrigerator is usually called a fridge.
fact: A refrigerator keeps food at about 3 to 5 degrees Celsius, which slows down bacteria.
fact: Raw meat goes on the bottom shelf of a refrigerator, so its juices cannot drip onto other food.
fact: A refrigerator moves heat from inside it to the outside.
exercise: «We put the milk back in the refrigerator.» What is a refrigerator? | A cupboard for plates and cups | *A kitchen machine that keeps food and drinks cool | A machine that washes clothes | A hot oven for baking bread
exercise: In everyday talk, people often call a refrigerator a ... | dishwasher | oven | toaster | *fridge
exercise: «Keep the cream refrigerated after you open it.» What does refrigerated mean here? | Left out in the sun to warm up | Cooked in a hot pan | Thrown away at once | *Kept cold in a refrigerator
test: Why does a refrigerator keep food at about 3 to 5 degrees Celsius? | It makes the food grow bigger | It stops the light from working | *It slows down bacteria, so food stays fresh longer | It makes the food hot so it tastes better
test: «Raw meat goes on the bottom shelf of the refrigerator.» Why is this a good rule? | The bottom shelf is the warmest part | *The meat cannot drip onto other food | Meat likes to be near the light | It makes the meat taste sweeter
exam: Which is a safe rule about refrigerators? | Hide in an old refrigerator for a game | *Never hide in an old refrigerator | Keep the door open all night for fun | Climb inside the refrigerator to find the cake
